    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nCopilot reviewed 5 out of 32 changed files in this pull request and generated 2 comments.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (1)</summary>\n\n**.github/actions/mise-setup/action.yml:57**\n* This composite action still forces Bundler to install into `vendor/bundle` and caches `vendor/bundle`, but the PR also sets `BUNDLE_PATH` in `.mise.toml` to `{{xdg_data_home}}/gem`. When `bin/setup` runs under `mise exec`, `BUNDLE_PATH` will typically override the local bundler config, so gems may be installed under `~/.local/share/gem` and the `vendor/bundle` cache will be ineffective.\n\nAlign the CI bundler configuration/cache with the new shared gem install location (or remove the `bundle config set --local path 'vendor/bundle'` step if it’s no longer intended).\n```\n    # Set bundler gem path before restoring the cache and before bin/setup,\n    # so bundle install (inside bin/setup) writes to the cacheable path.\n    - name: Set bundler PATH\n      shell: bash\n      run: bundle config set --local path 'vendor/bundle'\n    # Write toolchain preference to .toolchain-local so bin/setup (section 7)\n    # finds it and section 8 behaves correctly without prompting.\n    - name: Configure toolchain\n      shell: bash\n      run: |\n        if [[ \"${{ inputs.toolchain }}\" == \"true\" ]]; then\n          echo \"UDB_TOOLCHAIN_CONTAINER=1\" > .toolchain-local\n          echo \"UDB_TOOLCHAIN_CONTAINER=1\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n        else\n          echo \"UDB_TOOLCHAIN_NONE=1\" > .toolchain-local\n          echo \"UDB_TOOLCHAIN_NONE=1\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n        fi\n    # Docker Buildx must be available before bin/setup runs, because bin/setup\n    # section 8 may call _pull_or_build_toolchain_image which uses buildx in CI.\n    - name: Set up Docker Buildx\n      if: inputs.toolchain == 'true'\n      uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@8d2750c68a42422c14e847fe6c8ac0403b4cbd6f # v3.12.0\n    - name: Login to GHCR\n      if: inputs.toolchain == 'true'\n      uses: docker/login-action@c94ce9fb468520275223c153574b00df6fe4bcc9 # v3.7.0\n      with:\n        registry: ghcr.io\n        username: ${{ github.actor }}\n        password: ${{ github.token }}\n    # Restore all four caches BEFORE bin/setup runs.  bin/setup has idempotency\n    # guards in each section (bundle check, extconf.rb file checks, shared venv/npm\n    # directory checks, uv sync lockfile check) that skip work when the cache hit\n    # already populated the relevant paths.  This means bin/setup completes in\n    # seconds on a cache hit without any separate install steps.\n    - name: Cache bundler gems\n      uses: actions/cache@v4\n      with:\n        path: vendor/bundle\n        key: bundler-${{ runner.os }}-${{ hashFiles('.mise.toml', 'Gemfile.lock', 'tools/ruby-gems/*/Gemfile.lock', 'tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/Z3_VERSION', 'tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/ESPRESSO_VERSION', 'tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/EQNTOTT_VERSION', 'tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/MUST_VERSION') }}\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
